<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Library Borrowing Guide">
  <data key="d0">Library Borrowing Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A guide titled “Library Borrowing Guide.”&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Borrowing Guide provides instructions about borrowing and returning books, account eligibility, loan limits, loan periods, and due dates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Borrowing Guide provides instructions for renewing and returning a borrowed book.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Borrowing Guide provides instructions for checking titles, returning books, and renewing loans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Borrowing Guide provides instructions for renewing a borrowed book and handling a reservation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Borrowing Guide presents baseline borrowing rules and instructions for students.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bec09cbf50b78e30405fdc3229058fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Date">
  <data key="d0">Date</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A date is mentioned as something to check again.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bec09cbf50b78e30405fdc3229058fb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page 2 of 2">
  <data key="d0">Page 2 of 2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The text displays “2 / 2,” indicating the second page of two.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bec09cbf50b78e30405fdc3229058fb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Book">
  <data key="d0">Book</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A book is an item that can be borrowed and should be returned on or before its due date.&lt;SEP&gt;The book is the borrowed item that may be renewed or returned.&lt;SEP&gt;A book is an item that can be borrowed, returned by its due date, and renewed if it is not reserved.&lt;SEP&gt;The Book is the borrowed item that may be renewed if nobody else has reserved it.&lt;SEP&gt;A book is an item students may borrow, renew, and return.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Due Date">
  <data key="d0">Due Date</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A due date is the date by which each borrowed book should be returned.&lt;SEP&gt;The due date is the deadline by which a borrowed book should be returned and before which a renewal should be requested.&lt;SEP&gt;A due date is the date by which a borrowed book must be returned unless an eligible renewal applies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renewal">
  <data key="d0">Renewal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Renewal is the process described for extending a book's loan when nobody else has reserved it.&lt;SEP&gt;A renewal extends the borrowing period once by seven days when nobody else has reserved the book.&lt;SEP&gt;Renewal is the process of extending a book loan once for seven extra days when no other borrower has reserved the book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="My Loans">
  <data key="d0">My Loans</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">My Loans is the location where the new due date appears after renewal.&lt;SEP&gt;My Loans shows the due date for each borrowed book.&lt;SEP&gt;My Loans is the interface where a borrower can find a book and select the Renew option.&lt;SEP&gt;My Loans is a library account area where a borrower can find a book and view its updated due date.&lt;SEP&gt;My Loans is the account feature students use to check the due date for each title.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservation">
  <data key="d0">Reservation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A reservation determines whether the book can be renewed or must be returned by its original due date.&lt;SEP&gt;A reservation by another person prevents the described one-time, seven-day renewal.&lt;SEP&gt;A Reservation is another borrower's claim on a book and prevents renewal under the described instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Title">
  <data key="d0">Title</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A title identifies a book and should be checked separately according to the guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Extra Days">
  <data key="d0">Seven Extra Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven extra days is the loan extension available for a renewal.&lt;SEP&gt;Seven extra days is the additional borrowing period allowed by an eligible renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f74d3981177947bc583a0860d03ffe3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Borrowing And Returning Books">
  <data key="d0">Borrowing And Returning Books</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Borrowing and returning books are the activities covered by the Library Borrowing Guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Library Account Eligibility">
  <data key="d0">Library Account Eligibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Library account eligibility should be checked before borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loan Limit">
  <data key="d0">Loan Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The loan limit is listed in a table in the guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Loan Period">
  <data key="d0">Standard Loan Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The standard loan period is listed in a table in the guide.&lt;SEP&gt;The standard loan period is the baseline duration for borrowing a book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loan Information Table">
  <data key="d0">Loan Information Table</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The table lists the loan limit and standard loan period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afabfd0277eadab270f8c9f0d4f67b9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Original Due Date">
  <data key="d0">Original Due Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The original due date is the deadline for returning a reserved book.&lt;SEP&gt;The Original Due Date is the deadline by which a reserved book should be returned.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Due Date">
  <data key="d0">New Due Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The new due date is displayed in My Loans after a book is renewed.&lt;SEP&gt;The New Due Date is the updated deadline shown in My Loans after a successful renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renewal Steps">
  <data key="d0">Renewal Steps</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Renewal Steps is the caption of Figure 1, which presents steps for renewing a book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Result Confirmation">
  <data key="d0">Result Confirmation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Result confirmation is the instruction to verify the outcome of a renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b66dc4cdc65aee472efcef7cbf0db9</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Student Book Borrowing Limits and Standard Loan Period (table)">
  <data key="d0">Student Book Borrowing Limits and Standard Loan Period (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">The table states that students may borrow a maximum of 3 books at a time and that the standard loan period is 14 days. It supplies the baseline rules for the surrounding guidance on checking each book’s due date, returning books on time, and conditionally renewing once for 7 extra days when no other borrower has reserved the book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996573</data>
</node>
<node id="Library Book Renewal Steps Flowchart (image)">
  <data key="d0">Library Book Renewal Steps Flowchart (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">A three-step horizontal flowchart for renewing a library book: check the due date, find the book in My Loans, and renew it while checking the new due date. In the surrounding guide, renewal must be requested before the due date; eligibility and the updated due date should be checked.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996573</data>
</node>
<node id="Student">
  <data key="d0">Student</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A student is subject to the borrowing limits and procedures described in the guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Books at a Time">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Books at a Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The maximum books at a time rule sets the quantity of books a student may borrow simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3 Books">
  <data key="d0">3 Books</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Three books is the maximum number a student may borrow at one time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="14 Days">
  <data key="d0">14 Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourteen days is the standard loan period for a borrowed book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Student Account Eligibility">
  <data key="d0">Student Account Eligibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Student account eligibility is a condition students are instructed to check before borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renewal Rule">
  <data key="d0">Renewal Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The renewal rule allows a student to renew a book once for an extra seven days before its due date, provided nobody else has reserved it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="7 Extra Days">
  <data key="d0">7 Extra Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven extra days is the duration of the permitted renewal extension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Book Reservation">
  <data key="d0">Book Reservation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A reservation by another person prevents a student from renewing a book and requires return by the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604374813fb8c7f3a8154e53d151ad0b</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renewal Steps Flowchart">
  <data key="d0">Renewal Steps Flowchart</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Renewal Steps Flowchart visually summarizes checking the due date, finding the book in My Loans, renewing it, and checking the updated due date.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Before the Due Date">
  <data key="d0">Before the Due Date</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Before the Due Date is the time by which a borrower is instructed to check the loan and request a renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renew Command">
  <data key="d0">Renew Command</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Renew Command is the interface option the borrower clicks to request a book renewal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f4f0a32cfcf638b9c46120a873924cb</data>
  <data key="d4">library-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1794996602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
